From 27ee95ba62a22ff36803685e309c5a413dd5b2da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cctry <cctry@fb.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 17:37:23 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 22/38] [Memory] Borrow the DFLASH verify probabilities and
 rehearse them at startup

Give graph-pool borrowing a live consumer again. The full-vocabulary target
and draft probability matrices built in the DFLASH non-greedy accept path
die within their step, so their bytes come out of the graph pool's idle
storage. The kernel's cached chain buffers move above the scope: they
outlive the step, and correct_len aliases accept_token_num.

DFlashWorkerV2.prewarm_sampling rehearses that path at the largest verify
batch after graph capture. An undersized pool now surfaces at startup --
borrowing is retired and the measured footprint becomes post-capture KV
sizing headroom -- instead of OOMing under traffic.

Measured on Llama-3.1-8B + DFlash-UltraChat over 4x200 GSM8K examples per
arm: score 0.7525 (sd 0.021) and accept length 2.80, borrowing on or off.
